  "id": "Compound::DB00786 - Gene::118856",
  "verbalization": "Marimastat, a small molecule inhibitor, is shown to bind to multiple matrix metalloproteinases (MMPs) through distinct interactions with Mmp23b, Mmp26, and Mmp27. These MMPs are part of a broader pathway involving the matrix metalloproteinase family, which is known to play a critical role in extracellular matrix remodeling and tissue homeostasis. The shared participation of these MMPs in the same pathway and their common association with Mmp21 suggests a potential mechanistic link between Marimastat and Mmp21. The evidence indicates that Marimastat may inhibit Mmp21 through its interaction with these MMPs, potentially modulating their activity and downstream effects. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust and reliable relationship, supported by the shared biological context of MMPs and their involvement in Mmp21. This integrated evidence supports the hypothesis that Marimastat exerts its effects on Mmp21 through the inhibition of MMPs, highlighting a well-defined and biologically plausible mechanism.",
